#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:28
msgid ""
"Guido van Rossum named the language after *Monty Python's Flying Circus*, "
"not the snake -- hence the recurring \"spam\" and Monty Python references in"
" the docs."
msgstr ""
"Guido van Rossum puso al lenguaje el nombre de *Monty Python's Flying "
"Circus*, no de la serpiente; de ahí las recurrentes referencias a \"spam\" y"
" a Monty Python en la documentación."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:33
msgid "Who created the Python programming language?"
msgstr "¿Quién creó el lenguaje de programación Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:42
msgid "Linus Torvalds."
msgstr "Linus Torvalds."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:43
msgid "Dennis Ritchie."
msgstr "Dennis Ritchie."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:44
msgid "Guido van Rossum."
msgstr "Guido van Rossum."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:45
msgid "James Gosling."
msgstr "James Gosling."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:50
msgid ""
"Guido van Rossum started Python in late 1989 and released the first version "
"in 1991."
msgstr ""
"Guido van Rossum empezó Python a finales de 1989 y publicó la primera "
"versión en 1991."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:54
msgid "What does ``import this`` display?"
msgstr "¿Qué muestra ``import this``?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:67
msgid "A list of installed packages."
msgstr "Una lista de los paquetes instalados."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:68
msgid "The current date and time."
msgstr "La fecha y hora actuales."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:69
msgid "The Zen of Python."
msgstr "El Zen de Python."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:70
msgid "Nothing at all."
msgstr "Nada en absoluto."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:75
msgid ""
"``import this`` prints *The Zen of Python*, a short collection of guiding "
"aphorisms for writing Python code."
msgstr ""
"``import this`` imprime *El Zen de Python*, una breve colección de aforismos"
" que guían la escritura de código Python."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:79
msgid "In what year was Python first released?"
msgstr "¿En qué año se publicó Python por primera vez?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:96
msgid "Guido van Rossum published the first release of Python in 1991."
msgstr "Guido van Rossum publicó la primera versión de Python en 1991."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:99
msgid "Why do Python examples so often use the word \"spam\"?"
msgstr "¿Por qué los ejemplos de Python usan tan a menudo la palabra \"spam\"?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:108
msgid "It is an acronym for \"sample program\"."
msgstr "Es un acrónimo de \"sample program\"."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:109
msgid "It refers to unwanted email."
msgstr "Se refiere al correo no deseado."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:110
msgid "It is short for \"spa memory\"."
msgstr "Es una abreviatura de \"spa memory\"."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:111
msgid "It is a nod to a *Monty Python* sketch."
msgstr "Es un guiño a un sketch de *Monty Python*."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:116
msgid ""
"The classic placeholder names ``spam`` and ``eggs`` come from the *Monty "
"Python* \"Spam\" sketch, keeping with the language's namesake."
msgstr ""
"Los clásicos nombres de relleno ``spam`` y ``eggs`` provienen del sketch "
"\"Spam\" de *Monty Python*, en consonancia con el origen del nombre del "
"lenguaje."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:120
msgid "What is the standard file extension for Python source files?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cuál es la extensión de archivo estándar para los archivos fuente de "
"Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:129
msgid "``.pt``"
msgstr "``.pt``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:130
msgid "``.pyt``"
msgstr "``.pyt``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:131
msgid "``.py``"
msgstr "``.py``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:132
msgid "``.python``"
msgstr "``.python``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:137
msgid "Python source files use the ``.py`` extension."
msgstr "Los archivos fuente de Python usan la extensión ``.py``."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:140
msgid "Which major version of Python is actively supported today?"
msgstr "¿Qué versión principal de Python tiene soporte activo hoy en día?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:149
msgid "Python 1."
msgstr "Python 1."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:150
msgid "Python 2."
msgstr "Python 2."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:151
msgid "Python 3."
msgstr "Python 3."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:152
msgid "Python 5."
msgstr "Python 5."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:157
msgid ""
"Python 3 is the current, supported line. Python 2 reached end of life on "
"January 1, 2020."
msgstr ""
"Python 3 es la línea actual y con soporte. Python 2 llegó al final de su "
"vida útil el 1 de enero de 2020."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:161
msgid "What is the name of Python's official third-party package repository?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo se llama el repositorio oficial de paquetes de terceros de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:170
msgid "npm."
msgstr "npm."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:171
msgid "PyPI (the Python Package Index)."
msgstr "PyPI (el Python Package Index)."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:172
msgid "Maven Central."
msgstr "Maven Central."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:173
msgid "CRAN."
msgstr "CRAN."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:178
msgid ""
"PyPI, the Python Package Index, hosts the third-party packages you install "
"with ``pip``."
msgstr ""
"PyPI, el Python Package Index, aloja los paquetes de terceros que instalas "
"con ``pip``."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:182
msgid "What does ``import antigravity`` do?"
msgstr "¿Qué hace ``import antigravity``?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:195
msgid "Raises an ImportError."
msgstr "Lanza un ImportError."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:196
msgid "Disables Python's garbage collector."
msgstr "Desactiva el recolector de basura de Python."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:197
msgid "Prints the Zen of Python."
msgstr "Imprime el Zen de Python."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:198
msgid "Opens an *xkcd* webcomic in your browser."
msgstr "Abre un webcómic de *xkcd* en tu navegador."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:203
msgid ""
"``import antigravity`` is an Easter egg that opens the *xkcd* comic about "
"Python in your web browser."
msgstr ""
"``import antigravity`` es un huevo de pascua que abre en tu navegador el "
"cómic de *xkcd* sobre Python."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:207
msgid "Which line is genuinely part of the Zen of Python?"
msgstr "¿Qué frase forma parte realmente del Zen de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:216
msgid "\"Move fast and break things.\""
msgstr "\"Muévete rápido y rompe cosas.\""

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:217
msgid "\"Write once, run anywhere.\""
msgstr "\"Escríbelo una vez, ejecútalo donde sea.\""

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:218
msgid "\"Readability counts.\""
msgstr "\"La legibilidad cuenta.\""

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:219
msgid "\"There is more than one way to do it.\""
msgstr "\"Hay más de una forma de hacerlo.\""

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:224
msgid ""
"\"Readability counts.\" is one of the aphorisms in *The Zen of Python*. The "
"last one -- about many ways to do it -- is actually a Perl motto."
msgstr ""
"\"La legibilidad cuenta.\" es uno de los aforismos de *El Zen de Python*. El"
" último -sobre las muchas formas de hacerlo- es en realidad un lema de Perl."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:228
msgid "What is the default prompt of Python's interactive interpreter?"
msgstr "¿Cuál es el prompt por defecto del intérprete interactivo de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:237
msgid "``$``"
msgstr "``$``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:238
msgid "``>>>``"
msgstr "``>>>``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:239
msgid "``#``"
msgstr "``#``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:240
msgid "``py>``"
msgstr "``py>``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:245
msgid "The Python REPL prompts you with ``>>>`` for each new statement."
msgstr "El REPL de Python te muestra ``>>>`` para cada nueva instrucción."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:248
msgid "What does Python's logo depict?"
msgstr "¿Qué representa el logotipo de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:257
msgid "A single coiled snake."
msgstr "Una única serpiente enroscada."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:258
msgid "Two intertwined snakes."
msgstr "Dos serpientes entrelazadas."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:259
msgid "A circus tent."
msgstr "Una carpa de circo."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:260
msgid "A blue elephant."
msgstr "Un elefante azul."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:265
msgid ""
"The modern Python logo shows two stylized, intertwined snakes in blue and "
"yellow."
msgstr ""
"El logotipo moderno de Python muestra dos serpientes estilizadas y "
"entrelazadas en azul y amarillo."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:269
msgid "Python is best described as which kind of language?"
msgstr "¿Cómo se describe mejor Python como lenguaje?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:278
msgid "A markup language."
msgstr "Un lenguaje de marcado."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:279
msgid ""
"A language that must be compiled to a standalone ``.exe`` before running."
msgstr ""
"Un lenguaje que debe compilarse a un ``.exe`` independiente antes de "
"ejecutarse."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:280
msgid "An interpreted, high-level language."
msgstr "Un lenguaje interpretado y de alto nivel."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:281
msgid "A hardware description language."
msgstr "Un lenguaje de descripción de hardware."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:286
msgid ""
"Python is a high-level, interpreted language: you run source files directly "
"without a separate compile step."
msgstr ""
"Python es un lenguaje interpretado y de alto nivel: ejecutas los archivos "
"fuente directamente, sin un paso de compilación aparte."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:290
msgid ""
"Besides ``spam``, which word is the other classic Python placeholder name?"
msgstr ""
"Además de ``spam``, ¿cuál es el otro clásico nombre de relleno de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:299
msgid "``foo``"
msgstr "``foo``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:300
msgid "``bar``"
msgstr "``bar``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:301
msgid "``baz``"
msgstr "``baz``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:302
msgid "``eggs``"
msgstr "``eggs``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:307
msgid "``spam`` and ``eggs`` go together, both borrowed from *Monty Python*."
msgstr "``spam`` y ``eggs`` van juntos, ambos tomados de *Monty Python*."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:310
msgid "What is the name of the largest annual community Python conference?"
msgstr "¿Cómo se llama la mayor conferencia anual de la comunidad Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:319
msgid "PyDay."
msgstr "PyDay."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:320
msgid "SnakeConf."
msgstr "SnakeConf."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:321
msgid "PyCon."
msgstr "PyCon."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:322
msgid "DjangoCon."
msgstr "DjangoCon."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:327
msgid ""
"PyCon is the flagship community conference for Python, held in many "
"countries around the world."
msgstr ""
"PyCon es la conferencia comunitaria de referencia de Python, celebrada en "
"muchos países del mundo."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:331
msgid ""
"Complete the first line of the Zen of Python: \"Beautiful is better than "
"___.\""
msgstr "Completa la primera frase del Zen de Python: \"Bello es mejor que ___.\""

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:340
msgid "\"boring\"."
msgstr "\"aburrido\"."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:341
msgid "\"complex\"."
msgstr "\"complejo\"."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:342
msgid "\"clever\"."
msgstr "\"ingenioso\"."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:343
msgid "\"ugly\"."
msgstr "\"feo\"."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:348
msgid "The Zen of Python opens with \"Beautiful is better than ugly.\""
msgstr "El Zen de Python empieza con \"Bello es mejor que feo.\""

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:351
msgid "What does this program print?"
msgstr "¿Qué imprime este programa?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:364
msgid "``Hello world``"
msgstr "``Hello world``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:365
msgid "``Hello, world!``"
msgstr "``Hello, world!``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:366
msgid "``\"Hello, world!\"``"
msgstr "``\"Hello, world!\"``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:367
msgid "Nothing."
msgstr "Nada."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:372
msgid ""
"``print`` writes its argument to the screen exactly, including the comma and"
" exclamation mark."
msgstr ""
"``print`` escribe su argumento en la pantalla tal cual, incluyendo la coma y"
" el signo de exclamación."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:376
msgid "Which statement about Python's licensing is true?"
msgstr "¿Cuál de estas afirmaciones sobre la licencia de Python es cierta?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:385
msgid "It is proprietary and closed source."
msgstr "Es propietario y de código cerrado."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:386
msgid "It requires a paid license for commercial use."
msgstr "Requiere una licencia de pago para uso comercial."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:387
msgid "It is free and open source."
msgstr "Es libre y de código abierto."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:388
msgid "It can only be used for education."
msgstr "Solo puede usarse con fines educativos."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:393
msgid ""
"Python is free and open source, developed openly by the Python Software "
"Foundation and a global community."
msgstr ""
"Python es libre y de código abierto, desarrollado de forma abierta por la "
"Python Software Foundation y una comunidad global."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:397
msgid "Which of these is a real Python Easter egg?"
msgstr "¿Cuál de estos es un huevo de pascua real de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:406
msgid "``import pizza``"
msgstr "``import pizza``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:407
msgid "``import this``"
msgstr "``import this``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:408
msgid "``import rainbow``"
msgstr "``import rainbow``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:409
msgid "``import cake``"
msgstr "``import cake``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:414
msgid ""
"``import this`` prints *The Zen of Python*; the others are not real modules."
msgstr ""
"``import this`` imprime *El Zen de Python*; los demás no son módulos reales."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:417
msgid ""
"By what nickname was Guido van Rossum long known in the Python community?"
msgstr ""
"¿Con qué apodo se conoció durante mucho tiempo a Guido van Rossum en la "
"comunidad Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:426
msgid "The Architect."
msgstr "El Arquitecto."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:427
msgid "The Chief Snake."
msgstr "La Serpiente Jefa."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:428
msgid "The BDFL."
msgstr "El BDFL."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:429
msgid "The Grand Wizard."
msgstr "El Gran Mago."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:434
msgid ""
"Guido was the \"BDFL\" -- Benevolent Dictator For Life -- until he stepped "
"down from that role in 2018."
msgstr ""
"Guido fue el \"BDFL\" -Benevolent Dictator For Life, dictador benévolo "
"vitalicio- hasta que dejó ese cargo en 2018."
